  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Counter by pushing up",
  "description": "The pitch is split into three zones: each team has its own half and between them a narrow middle zone. Each team has its goalkeeper and four players in its own zone and a forward in the middle zone. Two players from the other team attack in your zone, so it is 2v5 with the goalkeeper, who always plays with the team that has the ball.\n\nThe team with more players must win the ball and counter through its forward in the middle zone. Two players – the forward and one who joins in – get across to the opponents' zone. There they are outnumbered, and the drill turns the other way. The two who lost the ball race straight back to their zone to help win it back. One of them stays in the middle zone as the new forward.\n\nYou can start more simply without opposition: the team makes three passes in its own half, plays up to the forward and four players push up into the other zone. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The first pass after winning the ball – forward to the forward if they are available."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Forward: get available before the ball is won, and turn if you can."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The player who joins in runs straight away, without waiting to see what happens."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball: run back on the shortest line and help the team win it back."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
